1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,580
Have you been traveling much?

3
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,880
I spent a couple years in the jungle south of the Dragon King Mountains.

4
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:38,940
Then I arrived at Eastport, where I met your father.

5
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:42,120
He was debating whether to send his daughters to join you.

6
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:45,620
So Ginger and I volunteered to help get them here.

7
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:47,800
Is Ginger in town right now?

8
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:51,280
Yes. She said she was returning to her prince.

9
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:53,060
You'll be glad to hear it.

10
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:55,200
I met your master, too.

11
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,920
Do you mean Master Roxy?

12
00:00:56,920 --> 00:01:02,760
Yes. Of course it wasn't my intention, but my third eye certainly terrified her.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,740
I can't say I'm surprised.

14
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:09,520
Roxy was the one who originally taught me to be afraid of the soup herd.

15
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:13,780
So, your trip. You got here awfully fast.

16
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,500
Your little sister was eager to arrive.

17
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:17,540
Which one?

18
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,100
Young Aisha, of course.

19
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:23,900
She proposed that we accompany a number of merchant caravans as guards.

20
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:25,700
So we made excellent time.

21
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:29,560
But it's been a long while since anyone ordered me around like that.

22
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,620
Sounds like she put you through it.

23
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:34,260
I'm actually not sure how to respond to that.

24
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:36,100
Laugh. It's funny.

25
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:41,140
Man, it really has been forever.

26
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,760
What did we used to talk about?

27
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:47,480
By the way, what happened to Aeris?

28
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:52,600
Things got complicated.

29
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,520
She decided to go her own way.

30
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:56,940
Is that so?

31
00:01:56,940 --> 00:02:02,300
I'm positive that wasn't a personal slight against you, Rudeus.

32
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:03,400
Yeah, right.

33
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,760
She said we weren't well-matched enough.

34
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,720
That could mean a lot of things.

35
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,440
Doesn't mean she hates you.

36
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:12,520
Have you considered that you may have misunderstood her intent?

37
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,240
I don't know.

38
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:15,000
Not really.

39
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,580
What else could she possibly have meant?

40
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:19,140
Wait for me?

41
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:23,260
Either way, I went through hell for three years without another word from her.

42
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:24,820
She didn't save me.

43
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:25,760
Sylphie did.

44
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,040
What's done is done.

45
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:30,580
Anyway, how long do you plan to be in town?

46
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,160
I leave tomorrow morning.

47
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:34,720
That's awfully sudden, isn't it?

48
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:35,440
Perhaps.

49
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:38,000
But I would rather not impose upon you.

50
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:39,900
What? You're not imposing?

51
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:46,540
Rudeus.

52
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:49,800
Don't look so despondent.

53
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,460
I'll come back again.

54
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:54,980
And Eris was never very good with words.

55
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,900
Try not to hold that against her too strongly.

56
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,360
If you meet again in the future,

57
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,600
keep a cool head and talk it out.

58
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:05,460
If I run into her first,

59
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:07,760
I'll try to get her side of things for you.

60
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:09,960
I'd appreciate it.

61
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:10,480
Thank you.

62
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:40,460
Thank you.

63
00:04:43,010 --> 00:04:45,010
Oh

64
00:05:13,010 --> 00:05:19,010
So that's how it is

65
00:05:26,610 --> 00:05:28,610
Rui Jared

66
00:05:30,810 --> 00:05:34,990
What was that about do you two know each other a long time ago?

67
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:42,190
They're both survivors of the Laplace war I bet that's left more than a few lasting grudges

68
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:46,930
Don't worry Rudeus. I have no intention of fighting him

69
00:05:47,650 --> 00:05:50,970
Although it is odd to see him here of all places

70
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:54,950
Tell me about it. He says he came here to meet me. Oh

71
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:58,930
I see I suppose that does fit his character

72
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:02,730
Well, it's time I got going

73
00:06:03,950 --> 00:06:06,190
Come inside. We'll make breakfast

74
00:06:13,010 --> 00:06:32,350
Well take care you too Rui Jared and good luck. Thanks again for all your help. We really appreciate it

75
00:06:32,890 --> 00:06:34,890
Hey Rui Jared

76
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:36,890
Thanks for your hard work

77
00:06:36,890 --> 00:06:42,350
You're welcome. Don't demand too much from Rudeus now. All right. I know I'll be good

78
00:07:12,350 --> 00:07:19,350
My daddy! And the woman that's living with him isn't the same lady as last time! How am I supposed to trust him?

79
00:07:19,350 --> 00:07:25,350
These things happen, Norn. That doesn't mean your brother is disloyal or faithless.

80
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:31,350
Forgive me. Remind me of your name one more time.

81
00:07:31,350 --> 00:07:34,350
Who, me? I'm Sylphiette.

82
00:07:34,350 --> 00:07:38,350
Miss Sylphiette, I leave all three of them in your care.

83
00:07:38,350 --> 00:07:40,350
Oh, of course.

84
00:07:42,350 --> 00:07:44,350
Well then, till next time.

85
00:07:56,350 --> 00:08:02,350
Okay, this is a little belated, but welcome home. Glad you made it safe.

86
00:08:02,350 --> 00:08:05,350
Thank you, and I'm glad to see you looking well too.

87
00:08:05,350 --> 00:08:13,350
Um, anyway, it might take a while to get used to living together again, but we'll figure it out.

88
00:08:13,350 --> 00:08:20,350
Yes, sir. And when did you get married to Sylphie? I had no idea that happened. Right? I bet you were surprised too, huh?

89
00:08:20,350 --> 00:08:24,350
I don't remember Sylphiette too well, actually.

90
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:32,350
Oh wait, brother! I almost forgot! Dad gave me a box of stuff for you to open as soon as we got here.

91
00:08:32,350 --> 00:08:34,350
Here you go!

92
00:08:42,350 --> 00:08:44,350
So what does Dad have to say?

93
00:08:44,350 --> 00:08:50,350
He included a copy of the letter he sent ahead of you, but this one is asking me to enroll you both in school.

94
00:08:50,350 --> 00:08:54,350
Why? I don't want to go to school! My mom taught me enough!

95
00:08:54,350 --> 00:08:56,350
You won't go?

96
00:08:56,350 --> 00:08:58,350
No! I want to be your maid!

97
00:08:58,350 --> 00:09:00,350
You promised I could!

98
00:09:00,350 --> 00:09:04,350
And look! I still carry this thing you gave me everywhere!

99
00:09:11,350 --> 00:09:16,350
Well, at least take the university's entrance exam, and we'll see how you score.

100
00:09:16,350 --> 00:09:18,350
Huh? Ah!

101
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:21,350
Okay, that's no problem!

102
00:09:21,350 --> 00:09:24,350
Do you want to sign up for it too, as long as we're at it?

103
00:09:24,350 --> 00:09:29,350
Answer him! Our brother is talking to you, Norn!

104
00:09:29,350 --> 00:09:33,350
I don't want to take it. I'm probably going to fail and I won't get in.

105
00:09:33,350 --> 00:09:39,350
Oh, you don't have to worry about getting in. We have the money. They'll admit anyone, as long as you can pay.

106
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:42,350
If you have to bribe them, then I don't want to go!

107
00:09:42,350 --> 00:09:48,350
I... no, sorry, I phrased that badly. I didn't mean I'm going to bribe them to let you in, I just meant tuition.

108
00:09:48,350 --> 00:09:52,350
Yeah, watch your mouth, Norn! You shouldn't speak to our big brother like that!

109
00:09:52,350 --> 00:09:55,350
But you heard what he said! He just wants to solve everything with money!

110
00:09:55,350 --> 00:09:58,350
That's only because you've been so bad at school your entire life!

111
00:09:59,350 --> 00:10:01,350
Fine, I'll take the stupid test!

112
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:04,350
Hey, where are you going? We're not done talking yet!

113
00:10:04,350 --> 00:10:05,350
Shut up!

114
00:10:09,350 --> 00:10:13,350
I just can't abide silky children. Don't you agree, big brother?

115
00:10:15,350 --> 00:10:16,350
Listen to me.

116
00:10:16,350 --> 00:10:17,350
Yes?

117
00:10:17,350 --> 00:10:20,350
I don't want to hear you talk down to your sister again.

118
00:10:20,350 --> 00:10:22,350
Why do you think it's okay to treat her that way?

119
00:10:22,350 --> 00:10:26,350
I don't know. It's just like she doesn't even try.

120
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:32,350
I understand that it may look that way to you, but she's doing her best. Give her a break.

121
00:10:33,350 --> 00:10:37,350
Well, I'll stop if you want me to. I promise.

122
00:10:37,350 --> 00:10:46,350
Aisha says she wants to be our maid instead of going to school. What do you think?

123
00:10:46,350 --> 00:10:52,350
It's true that we've been neglecting the house a bit lately, so if Aisha wants to help out, I would be happy to have her.

124
00:10:52,350 --> 00:10:57,350
I don't know. She's a kid. We have to be the adults here.

125
00:10:58,350 --> 00:11:04,350
Isn't it our whole job to, like, send her to school, broaden her horizons, all that kind of stuff?

126
00:11:04,350 --> 00:11:09,350
I do see what you're getting at, but I think you're underestimating her a little bit.

127
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:14,350
Aisha's a smart girl, and she'll do well for herself, whether she goes to school or not.

128
00:11:14,350 --> 00:11:15,350
Yeah.

129
00:11:15,350 --> 00:11:20,350
In which case, I would let her choose. Why overthink letting her follow her passion?

130
00:11:20,350 --> 00:11:31,350
I'm more worried about Norn, to be frank. She obviously misses your dad in Ruizyard. She seems very anxious. So we need to take extra good care of her.

131
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:32,350
Yeah. Agreed.

132
00:11:33,350 --> 00:11:40,350
I love that I can rely on Sylphie. She's almost like Fitz in that way. Or exactly like Fitz in that way.

133
00:11:40,350 --> 00:11:43,350
Was that bossy? Sorry if I sounded full of myself.

134
00:11:43,350 --> 00:11:49,350
Not at all. Thank you. You made perfect sense. I clearly don't know anything about little girls.

135
00:11:49,350 --> 00:11:52,350
So I'm gonna need your advice pretty often.

136
00:11:52,350 --> 00:11:57,350
Of course. That's what being married is all about. I love you.

137
00:11:57,350 --> 00:11:58,350
I know.

138
00:12:02,350 --> 00:12:03,350
Ta-da!

139
00:12:04,350 --> 00:12:06,350
Aisha, that's a perfect score.

140
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:11,350
Now I don't have to go to school, right? You said your decision depends on my exam score, remember?

141
00:12:11,350 --> 00:12:16,350
I sure did. Okay, go and work out your duties with Sylphie.

142
00:12:16,350 --> 00:12:17,350
Hooray!

143
00:12:17,350 --> 00:12:21,350
Didn't anticipate hiring a maid, much less a sister-shaped one.

144
00:12:23,350 --> 00:12:26,350
As for Norn, her score left something to be desired.

145
00:12:27,350 --> 00:12:32,350
She didn't do terribly, though. A little below average for her age group, but not bad.

146
00:12:32,350 --> 00:12:35,350
So tell me, you know what you want to study?

147
00:12:35,350 --> 00:12:41,350
I don't know all the options off the top of my head, but there are some fun intro classes.

148
00:12:41,350 --> 00:12:45,350
You could try a bunch of different things and pick later. Like, what if...

149
00:12:45,350 --> 00:12:50,350
Okay, then. I'll try living in the dorm.

150
00:12:54,350 --> 00:12:56,350
Not what I expected, but...

151
00:12:56,350 --> 00:13:02,350
Don't let her! Dad told us we had to come here and live with our big brother!

152
00:13:02,350 --> 00:13:08,350
Just shooting her down would be easy. But she did work up the courage to ask directly.

153
00:13:08,350 --> 00:13:13,350
Plus, she fights with Aisha and she can't stand me, so...

154
00:13:14,350 --> 00:13:16,350
Maybe we should give her a little space.

155
00:13:16,350 --> 00:13:20,350
If you're sure, then yeah. I think we can arrange that.

156
00:13:20,350 --> 00:13:24,350
That's not fair! Norn didn't even get a good score in her exam!

157
00:13:24,350 --> 00:13:26,350
Why does she get her way?

158
00:13:26,350 --> 00:13:30,350
I worked hard and I got everything right, so why does she get special treatment?

159
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:34,350
Relax, Aisha. I'm not humoring her or anything.

160
00:13:34,350 --> 00:13:39,350
The dorms could be a great environment for her. I won't keep her here if she's miserable.

161
00:13:40,350 --> 00:13:45,350
Are you being nicer to her because... because my mom was just a concubine?

162
00:13:46,350 --> 00:13:49,350
A concu... who told you that, Aisha?

163
00:13:50,350 --> 00:13:53,350
My mom told me, and Norn's grandma did too.

164
00:13:55,350 --> 00:13:58,350
Do you like Norn better than me because we're only half-related?

165
00:13:58,350 --> 00:14:00,350
I want to be your sister too!

166
00:14:03,350 --> 00:14:06,350
Aisha, hey! I don't consider Lilia a concubine.

167
00:14:06,350 --> 00:14:09,350
And you're just as much my little sister as Norn is.

168
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:12,350
But you're different people with different needs.

169
00:14:13,350 --> 00:14:15,350
I only want what's best for both of you.

170
00:14:18,350 --> 00:14:19,350
Okay, fine.

171
00:14:28,350 --> 00:14:45,350
Norn, just for my own peace of mind, I want to go over a few things before you start classes.

172
00:14:45,350 --> 00:14:49,350
The dorms have their own rules, so learn them and follow them.

173
00:14:50,350 --> 00:14:52,350
Study hard and be willing to ask questions.

174
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:54,350
And treat your friends right.

175
00:14:55,350 --> 00:14:57,350
If you can't commit to that, you'll have to commute from home.

176
00:14:57,350 --> 00:14:58,350
Okay.

177
00:14:59,350 --> 00:15:04,350
Next up, if you ever have any trouble at school, you can always come talk to me or Sylphie.

178
00:15:05,350 --> 00:15:06,350
Okay.

179
00:15:06,350 --> 00:15:09,350
And, uh, make sure you brush your teeth every morning and before you go to bed.

180
00:15:10,350 --> 00:15:11,350
Okay.

181
00:15:11,350 --> 00:15:12,350
Make sure to bathe regularly.

182
00:15:13,350 --> 00:15:14,350
Okay.

183
00:15:14,350 --> 00:15:15,350
Do all your homework on time.

184
00:15:16,350 --> 00:15:17,350
Okay.

185
00:15:17,350 --> 00:15:19,350
And try to keep yourself healthy.

186
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:23,350
Lastly, come visit us.

187
00:15:23,350 --> 00:15:25,350
I want to see you back every ten days or so.

188
00:15:26,350 --> 00:15:28,350
Okay, but why?

189
00:15:32,350 --> 00:15:33,350
Because I worry.

190
00:15:35,350 --> 00:15:36,350
Whatever you say.

191
00:15:48,350 --> 00:15:49,350
Hey, Norn.

192
00:15:50,350 --> 00:15:52,350
I'm so excited for our next class.

193
00:15:52,350 --> 00:15:54,350
I wonder which teacher we're gonna get.

194
00:16:03,350 --> 00:16:05,350
Norn's been at school for a month already.

195
00:16:06,350 --> 00:16:09,350
But I don't think she's made any friends yet and that's starting to worry me.

196
00:16:12,350 --> 00:16:14,350
You seem down lately, boss, you know that?

197
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:16,350
Do I look down?

198
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,350
Yeah, like the downest.

199
00:16:19,350 --> 00:16:22,350
So, we got you a little present to cheer you up, Meow.

200
00:16:23,350 --> 00:16:25,350
It took us a whole month to get it ready for you.

201
00:16:26,350 --> 00:16:27,350
Sounds like you went all out.

202
00:16:28,350 --> 00:16:29,350
Whoa there!

203
00:16:30,350 --> 00:16:31,350
No peeking till you get home, Meow.

204
00:16:32,350 --> 00:16:34,350
Open it in secret, or no one will catch you.

205
00:16:35,350 --> 00:16:37,350
Okay, this was fine and now I'm scared.

206
00:16:38,350 --> 00:16:39,350
But hey, thank you anyway.

207
00:16:40,350 --> 00:16:41,350
Yeah, don't mention it.

208
00:16:42,350 --> 00:16:43,350
Yeah, we'll do anything for you, boss.

209
00:16:46,350 --> 00:16:48,350
Whatever it is feels soft.

210
00:16:49,350 --> 00:16:50,350
Better not be mice.

211
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:52,350
May I ask what you're up to?

212
00:16:53,350 --> 00:16:54,350
Oh, nothing much.

213
00:16:55,350 --> 00:16:57,350
Trying to guess what's in this bag without opening it.

214
00:16:57,350 --> 00:16:58,350
Could you accompany me to the student council office?

215
00:16:58,350 --> 00:16:59,350
Oh, yeah, okay.

216
00:16:59,350 --> 00:17:00,350
Right behind you.

217
00:17:03,350 --> 00:17:04,350
Lovely to see you, highness.

218
00:17:04,350 --> 00:17:05,350
Is there something I can help you with?

219
00:17:05,350 --> 00:17:06,350
Yes, perhaps you can.

220
00:17:06,350 --> 00:17:10,350
Some new students in the girls dormitory have been a bit on edge lately.

221
00:17:10,350 --> 00:17:11,350
Oh?

222
00:17:11,350 --> 00:17:15,350
Upon investigation, most of the distress is among small-breasted girls with pretty faces.

223
00:17:16,350 --> 00:17:17,350
Don't tell me Norn got caught up in something bad.

224
00:17:18,350 --> 00:17:19,350
I'll help in any way I can.

225
00:17:19,350 --> 00:17:20,350
Whatever you need.

226
00:17:20,350 --> 00:17:21,350
Today, I'll help in any way I can.

227
00:17:21,350 --> 00:17:22,350
Whatever you need.

228
00:17:22,350 --> 00:17:23,350
Today, I was able to question one victim directly.

229
00:17:23,350 --> 00:17:24,350
Linia and Persina, it appears.

230
00:17:24,350 --> 00:17:25,350
Demanded the poor girl remove her underwear on the spot for them.

231
00:17:25,350 --> 00:17:26,350
Did they know?

232
00:17:26,350 --> 00:17:27,350
No.

